WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.410 --> 00:00:03.816
<v Examiner>Define an antidote, and give an example.

2
00:00:03.816 --> 00:00:04.418
<v Examiner>Two marks.

3
00:00:04.868 --> 00:00:07.436
The hook: naloxone blocks the opioid.

4
00:00:07.436 --> 00:00:10.351
N A C protects the liver from paracetamol.

5
00:00:10.801 --> 00:00:14.521
An antidote is a substance that counteracts a poison.

6
00:00:14.521 --> 00:00:17.820
Her slide gives four ways an antidote can work.

7
00:00:17.820 --> 00:00:21.400
One, binders, which reduce the level of free toxin.

8
00:00:21.400 --> 00:00:23.786
Activated charcoal is the example.

9
00:00:23.786 --> 00:00:27.366
Two, enzyme inhibition: slowing an enzyme's action.

10
00:00:27.366 --> 00:00:30.244
Three, enzyme activation: speeding it up.

11
00:00:30.244 --> 00:00:33.964
And four, blocking receptors, which is an antagonist.

12
00:00:33.964 --> 00:00:37.544
That word should ring a bell from pharmacodynamics:

13
00:00:37.544 --> 00:00:43.791
an agonist binds a receptor and causes a response, and an antagonist binds and blocks it.

14
00:00:45.241 --> 00:00:46.462
Her two examples.

15
00:00:46.462 --> 00:00:50.700
Naloxone, brand name Narcan, works as an opioid antagonist.

16
00:00:50.700 --> 00:00:55.441
It blocks the opioid receptors, so it reverses an opioid overdose.

17
00:00:55.441 --> 00:00:57.452
And N-acetylcysteine, N A C,

18
00:00:57.452 --> 00:01:02.480
reduces the production of the toxic metabolites made from paracetamol,

19
00:01:02.480 --> 00:01:05.785
so it's the antidote for paracetamol overdose.

20
00:01:06.235 --> 00:01:08.055
Where the marks go missing.

21
00:01:08.055 --> 00:01:10.886
Naloxone is an antagonist, not an agonist.

22
00:01:10.886 --> 00:01:14.122
It blocks the receptor, it doesn't stimulate it.

23
00:01:14.122 --> 00:01:17.560
And N A C doesn't remove paracetamol from the body.

24
00:01:17.560 --> 00:01:21.403
It reduces the toxic metabolites the liver makes from it.

25
00:01:21.853 --> 00:01:22.535
<v Examiner>Once more.

26
00:01:22.535 --> 00:01:23.218
<v Examiner>Antidotes.

27
00:01:25.668 --> 00:01:30.976
An antidote counteracts a poison: by binding it, like activated charcoal;

28
00:01:30.976 --> 00:01:36.866
by slowing or speeding an enzyme; or by blocking its receptors, as an antagonist.

29
00:01:36.866 --> 00:01:42.320
Naloxone, Narcan, is an opioid antagonist that reverses an opioid overdose.

30
00:01:42.320 --> 00:01:47.919
N-acetylcysteine, N A C, reduces the toxic metabolites made from paracetamol.
